{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/683765-bane-seals-bindings-outside-the-uktena","id":683765,"title":"Bane Seals/Bindings outside the Uktena","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-30T19:46:05-07:00","id":683765,"title":"Bane Seals/Bindings outside the Uktena","content":"I find the idea of Bane Seals and the Rite of Bane Binding to be useful concepts. I understand that they are associated with the Uktena, and the Bane Tenders camp. However, I find these concepts to be too useful to limit them to the Uktena. It seems to me every region of the world could have some horrible Bane trapped there, slowly becoming free. It is a great campaign hook, and it should be part of the toolkit of any WW ST.<br /> <br /> I think these Fetishes and Rites (or their equivalents) should be known among all the tribes. It's just that they are less well known than they are among the Uktena. Only a rare few members of the other tribes learn these secrets because of how dangerous they are. Exceptional Silver Fangs, Silent Striders, Shadow Lords, Fianna, etc. do learn them. It's just that only the Uktena totem encourages his children to learn these things because of his nature.<br /> <br /> Has anyone else done this in their campaigns?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T20:25:05-07:00","id":683834,"title":"","content":"In my world rites of Bane binding are pretty common among the Nations. Every tribe has this &quot;too mighty to destroy&quot; Banes stored about. the Silver Fangs got the Zmei, the Shadow Lords Kuppala and so on.<br /> <br /> the Rites are not considered Tainted knowledge in this world but the Uktena art, that enables to redirect the energy of the Bane to productive uses or at least not turn the area around the prison a spiritual desert is dangerous because it needs constant contact with the evil spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2225-ganonso","name":"ganonso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T01:41:53-07:00","id":684091,"title":"","content":"Everyone can bind Banes, some times it's the only way to actually keep a bane away. As Ganonso has mentioned there are imprisoned banes (And Other Things) all over the world with all the tribes being involved. Off the top of my head - The Fianna and the Fomorarch, Silver Fangs and the Zmei, Shadow Lords and Kupala and Silent Striders and whatever the things in the desert were mentioned in Rage accross Egypt.<br /> <br /> The Uktena are known for it because they actually imprisoned a large number of horribly powerful banes all accross the Americas and have a wow to make sure those things stay aslep and don't go free.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T04:39:51-07:00","id":684254,"title":"","content":"I personally never liked that Summoning and Binding were handled in 2 Rites in WtA. I like to incorporate a lot more linear magik from the Sorcerer book into my chronicles. So there are actually a lot of summoning, binding, and even warding rites used for this kind of topic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}